            <ArticleTitle>Echocardiography in differential diagnosis of chest pain and elevated cardiac biomarkers: a case of cardiac angiosarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>406-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/ejechocard/jer030</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angiosarcoma is the most common primary cardiac malignancy with a poor prognosis. In this report, we describe a 28-year-old male patient presenting with symptoms and findings of myocardial ischaemia who has been finally diagnosed with cardiac angiosarcoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
